    // if interfaceId equals type(IAccessControl).interfaceId OR type(IERC165).interfaceId.
    // We express this by checking that when interfaceId equals either of those two well-known ids,
    // supportsInterface returns true. The mutant using && will return false for those ids and
    // therefore the test will fail on the mutant for some fuzzed inputs (specifically those ids).
